= 1923 <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#87CEFA;">Partito Popolare Italiano</span> Congress

The <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#87CEFA;">Partito Popolare Italiano</span>, known also as the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#87CEFA;">PPI</span> or the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#87CEFA;">Italian People's Party</span> have begun their fourth Congress. It's two factional bloc, with Sturzo on the left-wing of the party and De Gasperi's moderate-wing of the party is still prominent, but it seems the the right-wing of the party, represented by the Triumvirate has gained significant power within the party as well.

While Sturzo commands the support of the Christian Democrats and the 'White' <span style="color:#C0DCED;">Peasant Leagues</span>, De Gasperi is supported by Moderate Clericalists and the Clergy. On the other hand, the Triumvirate is supported by Hardliner Clericalists & the <span style="color:#522A00">National</span>-<span style="color:#0047AB;">Conservatives</span> of the party.

- @ppi_fourth: The party votes...

@ppi_fourth
go-to: sturzo_1923 if ppi_left >= ppi_moderates and ppi_left >= ppi_right; gasperi_1923 if ppi_moderates > ppi_left and ppi_moderates >= ppi_right; triumvirate_1923 if ppi_right > ppi_left and ppi_right > ppi_moderates

@sturzo_1923
face-image: img/portraits/LuigiSturzo.jpg
on-arrival: ppi_left += 2; ppi_relation += 2; ppi_leader = "Sturzo"

It seems the progressives have managed to sway the party, as Luigi Sturzo is elected Secretary General of the party once again, re-continuing the party's collaborative policies with the left.

@gasperi_1923
face-image: img/portraits/DeGasperi.jpg
on-arrival: ppi_relation -= 7; ppi_leader = "De Gasperi"; ppi_moderates += 2;

Alcide De Gasperi, with his support base, has been elected the fourth Secretary General of the Party. Representing a turn from the left, the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#87CEFA;">PPI</span> will cooperate further with the <span style="color:#0047AB;">libe</span><span style="color:#FFD700;">ral</span> parties.

@triumvirate_1923
on-arrival: ppi_right += 2; ppi_leader = "Triumvirate"; ppi_relation -= 10;

Shockingly, the Triumvirate have been able to achieve a plurality, establishing a joint Vice-Secretariat Position of the three. This represents a sharp turn from the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#87CEFA;">PPI</span>'s roots, and we should assume the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#87CEFA;">PPI</span> will be willing to cooperate with the <span style="color:#3D3D3D;">fascists</span>.

- @root: Damn it.